      "message": "use \u0027mNumMallocs\u0027 for member field, but the thing is, this will override previous values, and you have to clear out the state.\n\nAlso, nit: Consider something like:\n\n```\nstruct State {\n   std::vector\u003csize_t\u003e expectedMallocs;\n};\nauto state \u003d std::make_shared\u003cState\u003e();\nreturn OnMalloc([state\u003dstate](size_t bytes) {\n    state-\u003eexpectedMallocs;\n});\n```\n\nThat way, it\u0027s owned by the lambda. In this way, you can also avoid subclassing \u0027Test\u0027 and TEST_F, so that they are all raw tests (and no one is tempted to add shared \u0027SetUp\u0027 etc..",
